<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Halifax rated &quot;long-term buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Halifax rated &quot;long-term buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Halifax Plc, the banking group which made its market debut on Monday, was rated &quot;long-term buy&quot; at HSBC James Capel, analysts at the brokerage said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Capel comment came in a review of the bank sector, which has been been highly volatile in recent sessions as some investors cashed in on this year's strong gains to finance the purchase of Halifax shares.</p>
<p>Further detail on the Capel rating was not immediately available.</p>
<p>Halifax shares were down 18-1/2p at 716 by 1056 GMT in active trade of 12.8 million shares.</p>
<p>Earlier Goldman Sachs said it began coverage of Halifax shares were a &quot;market underperformer&quot; rating.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
